OL,3,CCould you be fined #1,000 for filling
OL,4,Cup your paddling pool?
OL,6,FThese weather conditions mean more
OL,7,Fthan 20 million people are currently
OL,8,Fliving under hosepipe bans to help
OL,9,Fprotect drinking water supplies.
OL,11,FAccording to the Environment Agency,
OL,12,Fusing a hosepipe can require 1,000
OL,13,Flitres an hour ` which is more than a
OL,14,Ffamily-of-four will use in a day.
OL,16,FBut what are the rules surrounding a
OL,17,Fhosepipe ban, who do they apply to,
OL,18,Fand what could happen if you break
OL,19,Fthem?
OL,21,FWhere are hosepipe bans in effect?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30503
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785779366
OL,3,CCould you be fined #1,000 for filling
OL,4,Cup your paddling pool?
OL,6,FSeven water companies across the
OL,7,Fcountry have introduced restrictions
OL,8,Fofficially known as a "Temporary Use
OL,9,FBan" (TUB). These are:
OL,11,FYour water bill should tell you who
OL,12,Fsupplies your water services, but you
OL,13,Fcan also check the government's
OL,14,Finteractive map. You could only be at
OL,15,Frisk of prosecution if the ban is in
OL,16,Fplace where you live.
OL,18,FWhat does a temporary use ban prevent
OL,19,Fme from doing?
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
